      "groups": [
        {
          "id": "cet4-paper-2021121-part-3-section-1-group-1",
          "title": "Questions 26 to 35 are based on the following passage.",
          "presentation": "reading",
          "instructions": [],
          "stimulusBlocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Many people believe that passion and commitment are the foundations of strong romantic relationships. But a relationship is made of two "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2021121-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-26"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " individuals. And the personality traits (特， 性 ) these individuals "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2021121-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-27"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " or lack can often make a relationship more- or less- likely to "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2021121-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-28"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " . Recent research has found that one trait in particular 一 humility (#5b) - is an important indicator of successful relationships. Humility can sometimes be "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2021121-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-29"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " with a lack of confidence. But researchers have come to realize that being humble generally indicates the "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2021121-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-30"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " of deeply admirable personal qualities. Being humble means you have the ability to accurately "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2021121-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-31"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " your deficiencies without denying your skills and strengths. For example, you might recognize that you are intelligent, but realize that you are not a "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2021121-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-32"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " . Thus, humility leads to an honest view of one's own advantages and shortcomings. Humble people do not ignore, avoid, or try to deny their limits or deficiencies. They can "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2021121-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-33"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " mistakes, see value in things that are far from perfect and identify areas for improvement. Perhaps it is not "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2021121-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-34"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " , then, that humility appears to be a huge asset to relationships. One study found that people tend to rate this quality "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2021121-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-35"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " in their spouse. The study also found that someone who is humble is more likely to initiate a romantic relationship, perhaps because they are less likely to see themselves as \"too good“ for someone else. Thus, a humble partner might be your ideal partner."
                }
              ]
            }
